00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.159
Understanding the Economy in 30 Minutes The

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:06.680
"mechanisms" of the economy are simple, but

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.390
few people understand them,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.490
and

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.150
many are driven into economic hardship because they cannot accept these "mechanisms."

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.249
So today, I'd like to

00:00:18.249 --> 00:00:22.049
explain the "mechanisms" of the economy in a simple and concrete way.

00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:25.320
This is an unconventional approach, but it has been

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.150
proven correct for over 30 years, and that is why

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.460
I was able to predict and avoid the global financial crisis.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.260
Okay, let's begin.  The

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.520
economic system may seem complex, but its mechanism is actually quite simple.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.930
This consists of simple components and simple transactions.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.260
This has been happening over and over again.  It is

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.460
human nature that drives transactions.  From

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.800
here, three main elements that drive the economy emerge.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.120
The first is the growth of productive forces.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.650
The second is the short-term cycle of debt. The

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.400
third is the long-term cycle of debt.  By

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.770
considering these three elements individually and then building a model that combines them

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.530
, we can understand economic trends and the

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.590
current situation.  Let's

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.830
start by looking at the simplest element of economics:

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.860
transactions.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.840
Simply put, economics is a series of transactions, and

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.570
transactions are simple things.  We do

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.360
business with each other all the time.  A

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.760
transaction occurs when you buy something.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.240
In a transaction, the buyer provides money and credit,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.150
and in exchange, the

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:42.550
seller provides goods, services, assets, etc.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.150
Credit is like money, so if you

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:49.280
add up the money you spent and the credit you used, you'll know the total

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.160
amount you owe.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.560
This total payment amount drives the economy.  Dividing the

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.590
payment amount

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.990
by the sales volume will give you the unit

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.290
price.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:04.380
This is the transaction.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.110
These are components of the economic system.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:12.019
Economic waves and movements are driven by transactions.

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:14.469
Therefore, if you understand transactions, you

00:02:14.469 --> 00:02:16.569
can understand how the economy works.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.510
Economic markets are comprised of transactions between buyers and

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.510
sellers

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.910
.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.540
For example, the wheat market, the

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.840
automobile market, the

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:27.640
stock market

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.550
, and other markets.  The

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.470
economy is the sum of all transactions and all markets

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.670
.  By calculating the total

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.550


00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.450
amount paid and

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.430
total sales across all markets

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.030
, we

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.630
can understand how the economy works.  It's

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.960
simple.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.430
People, companies, banks, government agencies.  All of this is related to the

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.730
deal I just mentioned.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.530
Money and credit are exchanged for goods, services, and assets.  The

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.500
largest buyers and sellers are government agencies.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.040
This can be classified into two categories.  The

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.690
central government collects taxes and spends money.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.669
And then there's the central bank, which,

00:03:09.669 --> 00:03:12.269
unlike ordinary buyers and sellers,

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:15.989
can control the total amount of money and credit in the economy.  In other words, the

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:19.650
central bank can control interest rate movements

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.020
and print new currency.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.620
Therefore,

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.200
central banks have a significant influence on the flow of credit

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.700
.  Let's

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.629
consider credit.

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:34.659
Credit is a crucial element of the economy, but it's

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:36.539
also one of the least understood.

00:03:37.039 --> 00:03:40.319
This is the largest and most volatile

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:42.100
element of the economy, making it the most important.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.100
Just as buyers and sellers trade in the market,

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.969
lenders and borrowers also trade.

00:03:49.969 --> 00:03:53.569
Lenders want to increase their cash reserves, while

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:57.260
borrowers want to buy more than they have on hand, such as a

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.059
house or a car, or

00:03:59.059 --> 00:04:02.319
start a business or make investments.

00:04:03.019 --> 00:04:04.599
Credit can help both lenders and

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:07.799
borrowers.  The

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:11.560
borrower promises to repay the borrowed amount, i.e., the principal,

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.719
plus interest

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.419
.

00:04:15.419 --> 00:04:17.560
High interest rates make the

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.560
burden heavy, leading to a decrease in the amount borrowed.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.540
On the other hand, if interest rates are low, the

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.040
amount borrowed will increase.  Credit is generated when

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.930
the borrower promises to repay and the

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.959
lender believes that promise

00:04:29.959 --> 00:04:31.059
.

00:04:31.659 --> 00:04:35.170
Regardless of who the two people are, they can generate credits.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.210
This may seem simple, but there's

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.499
another side to the credits.  When

00:04:40.499 --> 00:04:43.599
credit is incurred,

00:04:43.599 --> 00:04:45.029
debt is incurred.

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:48.670
Debt is an asset for the lender and a

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.770
liability for the borrower.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.540
In the future, when

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.240
the borrower repays the principal and interest, the

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.549
assets and liabilities will be extinguished and the

00:04:58.549 --> 00:05:00.949
transaction will be settled.

00:05:01.749 --> 00:05:04.629
So why is credit important?  When

00:05:05.229 --> 00:05:07.619
borrowers gain credit, they can

00:05:07.619 --> 00:05:09.719
increase their spending.

00:05:09.719 --> 00:05:13.349
Spending boosts the economy.  Because

00:05:13.349 --> 00:05:15.699
one person's expenses become

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:17.099
another person's income.  Please think about it

00:05:17.499 --> 00:05:22.189
.  Your expenses become someone else's income.  The

00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:25.279
income you earn comes from someone else's expenses.

00:05:25.279 --> 00:05:29.149
Therefore, when your spending increases, someone else's income increases.

00:05:29.149 --> 00:05:32.649
When someone's income increases,

00:05:32.649 --> 00:05:34.649
lenders tend to increase the amount they lend.

00:05:34.649 --> 00:05:37.629
Because the borrowers' creditworthiness has increased.

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:40.929
Credit borrowers

00:05:40.929 --> 00:05:43.519
have the ability to repay and collateral.  If your

00:05:44.319 --> 00:05:48.319
income is greater than your debt, your ability to repay it increases.

00:05:49.079 --> 00:05:55.749
Even if you can't repay the loan, if the collateral has a high value, it can be sold.

00:05:55.749 --> 00:06:00.340
This allows lenders to lend with peace of mind.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.960
As your income increases, you can borrow more and

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.680
increase your spending.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.920
One person's expenses become another person's income, which

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.360
means they can borrow more.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.350
This positive cycle leads to economic growth.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.640
This will create an economic wave.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.620
In a transaction, you need to offer something in exchange for something else, and the

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.830
amount you receive depends on how much you can produce

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.430
.  The

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:34.680
accumulation of knowledge raises living standards and

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.930
increases productivity.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.430
Inventors and workers are

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.540
lazy and do nothing, so their

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.950
productivity and standard of living are higher.

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:49.710
However, this might not be the case in the short term.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:54.340
Productivity is an important factor in the long term, but credit plays a crucial role in the short term.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.370
Productivity doesn't fluctuate much in the short term.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.480
Therefore, it has little impact on economic fluctuations.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:06.750
However, by using debt, it is possible to make consumption exceed production.  On the

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.050
other hand, when making repayments, you will have to reduce your spending.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.770
Debt has two major cycles.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:20.830
One cycle is 5 to 8 years, and the other is 75 to 100 years.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:25.160
Normally, even if you can feel the movement of these waves, you don't notice that they have a period.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.490
Wave movements occur daily and weekly, making it difficult to notice larger movements.  Let's take

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.950
a step back and examine these three major elements, and

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:37.000
consider how their interactions affect the economy.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:42.340
Minor fluctuations in economic trends are not caused by economic revolutions or changes in the employment environment.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.240
This fluctuation is influenced by the amount of credit available.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.070
Imagine an economy where credit does not exist.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.810
Here, the only way to increase spending is to

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.480
increase income.  In

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:59.080
other words, we need to increase productivity and working hours.  The

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:03.020
economy cannot grow without increasing production.

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.250
My spending is someone else's income, so if

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:10.430
our productivity increases, the economy can grow.  In

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.530
this environment, economic growth

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.910
occurs simultaneously with productivity growth.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.780
However, if it becomes possible to rent it, the waves will fluctuate.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.900
This is not caused by any laws or regulations.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:27.660
This is based on human nature and is also caused by fluctuations in credit.  Taking out a

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:32.270
loan is, in a sense, bringing your expenses forward.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:37.479
To make purchases that exceed your income, you will have to spend more than you earn.

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:41.460
To make this possible, you need to borrow money from your future self.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.610
This way, in the future, you will need to

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:48.690
reduce your expenses to less than your income in order to repay the debt.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.950
This causes the waves to move up and down.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.400
Basically, borrowing money will cause fluctuations in your finances.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:59.950
This is true for both individuals and the economy as a whole.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.850
Therefore, it is essential to have a solid understanding of credits.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.590
When credit is generated, it

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:08.790
triggers a predictable series of events in the future.  In

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.570
this sense, credit is different from money.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:14.580
Money is used to settle transactions.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:18.120
When you buy beer with cash at a bar, the

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.800
transaction is settled on the spot.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.630
However, if you buy beer using a credit card, you'll

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:24.730
incur a "credit" charge.  The

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.530
promise is that it will be repaid in the future.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:32.070
You and the bar will end up creating both assets and liabilities.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.250
Credits appeared out of nowhere.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:38.900
These assets and liabilities will be

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.250
extinguished when the "debt" is paid later.  The

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.550
"debt" is resolved, and the

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.090
transaction is settled.  In

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:50.250
reality, most of what we commonly consider money is actually credit.  The total

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:55.510
amount of credit in the United States is approximately $50 trillion, but the

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:59.680
total amount of money in circulation is only about $3 trillion.  In an

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.040
economy without credit

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:05.200
, spending will not increase unless production increases.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.280
However, in a credit-based economy,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.780
spending can be increased by taking on more debt.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:14.120
Therefore, in a credit-based economy, spending can be greater, and

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:18.090
income growth can outpace productivity.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.890
However, this is a short-term phenomenon and will not occur in the long term.  Please don't

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.360
misunderstand this point.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:25.660
Credit isn't necessarily a bad thing that simply causes economic fluctuations.  Things

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:30.900
get worse when consumption becomes excessive and repayment becomes impossible.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:34.490
However, it can be a positive factor when it allows economic resources to be used to generate income and make it

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:37.690
possible to repay debts.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.980
For example, if you take out a loan to buy a television, you do not

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.879
generate any income to repay the loan.

00:10:44.079 --> 00:10:47.880
But if you take out a loan to buy a tractor,

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.560
increase your harvest, and boost your sales, you can

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.090
repay your debts and

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.490
improve your standard of living at the same time.  Let's look at

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.600


00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.600
how credit

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.300
generates economic growth in an economy where credit exists.  Let's

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.680
consider an example.  Let's

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.190
assume your annual income is $100,000 and your debt is zero.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:11.540
Because you have good credit, you

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.040
can, for example, borrow $10,000 using a credit card.  This means that

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.250
even with an income of $100,000, you

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.250
can spend $110,000.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.460
Your expenditure is someone else's income, meaning

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:24.460
that person earned $110,000.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:27.670
If this person has no debt and an income of $110,000, they

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:31.429
can borrow $11,000 and spend $121,000

00:11:31.429 --> 00:11:34.070
even with an income of $110,000

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:38.170
.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.640
Since this person's spending contributes to other people's income, by the

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.430
same principle, we can see that

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.430
this further boosts the economic tide

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.430
.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.600
But there's something we mustn't forget.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.809
Even if debt raises the height of economic fluctuations, those fluctuations will eventually subside.

00:11:56.009 --> 00:11:59.710
This represents the short-term cycle of debt.  As

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:04.380
economic activity increases and the economy expands,

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:06.840
short-term debt fluctuations begin.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:10.720
This leads to further increases in spending, and prices begin to rise.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:15.230
This is because the economy was boosted by credit.

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.450
This credit appeared out of nowhere.  When

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:22.680
spending and revenue increase faster than output,

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.880
prices begin to rise.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:28.000
Rising prices lead to inflation.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.500
Central banks want to avoid these problems, so they try to

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.010
prevent inflation and

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:38.250
raise interest rates when they sense prices rising.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:42.959
When interest rates rise, the number of people who can borrow money decreases.

00:12:42.959 --> 00:12:45.600
This will also increase the cost of existing debt.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.100
This means your credit card payment amount will increase.  With

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:54.459
fewer people borrowing and repayment costs soaring, the

00:12:54.459 --> 00:12:58.720
average citizen's spending will decrease.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.779
Since expenses are someone else's income,

00:13:02.779 --> 00:13:06.589
overall income will decrease.

00:13:06.589 --> 00:13:10.800
When spending decreases, prices also decrease.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.689
This is deflation.

00:13:12.689 --> 00:13:17.460
Economic activity will contract, leading to a recession.  When the

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.060
