value of assets is also increasing.

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.550
Stock prices are also soaring.  It's a

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:02.480
boom.  In situations like

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:06.690
these, borrowing money to buy goods, services, or assets is a

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.390
good strategy.  When

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:11.770
this trend becomes widespread in society, it creates a bubble.  If your

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:14.640
debt increases but your

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:18.110
income increases by the same amount, you won't have any problems repaying it.  Let's

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:21.970
call the ratio of debt to income the debt burden ratio.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:25.210
As long as income is increasing, there is no

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.040
problem with the debt burden ratio.  The

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:30.230
value of assets will also skyrocket.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:33.230
People take on large amounts of debt to

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.060
invest in assets.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.660
This will further increase the price.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.260
People feel wealthy.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:43.260
Even if your debt is ballooning, your

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:49.490
income and asset values ​​are increasing, so there's no risk in taking out credit.

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.530
But this won't last long, and it won't last

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.250
long.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:16:00.520
Over decades, the amount of debt gradually increases, and the amount of repayment also increases.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:05.400
Then, the time comes when your repayment amount increases faster than your income.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.240
As a result, people will reduce their spending.

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:12.200
Since one person's spending contributes to another person's income,

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.500
income levels will start to decline. This will make it more

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:19.020
difficult to borrow money, leading to a contraction of spending.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.020
Since debt repayments will continue,

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.440
expenses will decrease even further.  This is when the

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:27.140
waves of economic fluctuations "relapse" occur.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:30.960
This marks the peak of the long-term debt cycle.  The

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.150
debt burden became unsustainable.  This happened in

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:38.830
the United States, Europe, and other regions in

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.760
2008.  For the

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.430
same reason, it happened in Japan in 1989 and in the

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:48.750
United States in 1929.  When

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:51.980
this happens, leverage loses its momentum.

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:56.500
As a result, expenses will start to decrease.  As

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.540
incomes shrink, credit disappears, and

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.700
asset prices plummet, banks will struggle.  The

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:06.340
stock market crashes, social tensions rise, and

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:09.709
this vicious cycle repeats itself.  When

00:17:09.709 --> 00:17:13.850
income decreases and debt repayments increase,

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:17.990
borrowers are shut out,

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:22.360
credit dries up, and borrowers are

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:23.600
unable to borrow money to repay their debts.  As a result

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:28.440
, assets will be sold off, and the

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.550
market will be flooded with assets being put up for sale.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:36.370
Then the stock market crashes, the

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:39.740
real estate market collapses, and banks face difficulties.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:44.940
When asset value decreases, the value of collateral also shrinks, making it

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.280
even more difficult to borrow money.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.200
People feel poor, their

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:55.010
credit evaporates, their

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:55.890
spending decreases, their income decreases, their

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.890
asset values ​​decrease, their

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:58.590
credit decreases, and it

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.800
becomes even more difficult to borrow.  It's a

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.000
vicious cycle.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.530
This may seem similar to an economic downturn, but it's different.

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:10.160
Lowering interest rates does not necessarily lead to economic recovery.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:14.590
During an economic downturn, lowering interest rates will increase the amount people borrow.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:18.570
However, since leverage has disappeared, even if you try to lower interest rates, they are

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.530
already low, and

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:25.310
sometimes even drop to zero percent.  Therefore, economic recovery is impossible.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.210
Interest rates in the United States fell to zero percent in the 1930s when leverage disappeared

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.840
,

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.440
and again in 2008.  The difference between a

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.840
recession and the disappearance of leverage is that in the

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:40.270
latter case, the burden on borrowers

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.930
becomes excessively large.

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:45.050
This situation cannot be recovered even by lowering interest rates.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:50.240
Borrowers face the reality that they may not be able to repay the full amount.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:55.310
The borrower loses the ability to repay the loan, and the collateral loses its value.  I can't

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:59.370
bear the weight of my debt, and I don't have the energy to borrow any more.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:03.490
Lenders stop lending, and borrowers give up on borrowing.  The

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:07.020
value of the economy has essentially disappeared.

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.000
This applies to individuals as well.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.600
So what should you do when leverage disappears?  We must

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:17.540
reduce our unbearably large debt burden.  There

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.790
are four ways to do this.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:24.489
1.  1. People, businesses, and governments cut spending.  The

00:19:24.489 --> 00:19:28.409
debt will be defaulted on and restructured.

00:19:28.409 --> 00:19:34.139
3.  Assets are redistributed from the wealthy to everyone else,

00:19:34.139 --> 00:19:37.980
and then 4.  The central bank prints new banknotes.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:42.999
These four things actually happen when leverage disappears.

00:19:45.699 --> 00:19:47.779
Typically, spending is the first thing to be reduced.

00:19:47.879 --> 00:19:52.129
Individuals, businesses, and governments tighten their purse strings,

00:19:52.129 --> 00:19:54.869
cut spending, and try to pay off debt.

00:19:54.869 --> 00:19:58.559
This is called austerity.  It's easy to assume that when

00:19:58.559 --> 00:20:01.830
borrowers stop borrowing and

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:06.769
start paying off old debts, the debt burden ratio will decrease, but

00:20:06.769 --> 00:20:10.720
the opposite actually happens.  Because expenses decrease, and

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:14.610
expenses are a source of income for others, so

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:19.029
income shrinks.  Income shrinks faster than debt repayment.  This leads to a

00:20:19.029 --> 00:20:23.210
worsening of the debt burden ratio.  As I've said

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:26.330
before, a decrease in spending leads to deflation.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.389
Businesses try to cut costs, which leads to

00:20:29.389 --> 00:20:32.779
fewer jobs and more unemployment.

00:20:32.779 --> 00:20:37.139
This would necessitate further reductions in debt.

00:20:37.139 --> 00:20:41.149
Many borrowers are unable to repay their debts.  The

00:20:41.149 --> 00:20:44.299
borrower's debt is the lender's asset.

00:20:44.299 --> 00:20:48.749
When borrowers are unable to repay their loans to banks, people become worried about the money they have deposited and rush

00:20:48.749 --> 00:20:50.309
to banks to withdraw it, making it

00:20:50.309 --> 00:20:54.909
difficult for banks to operate. This makes it impossible for

00:20:54.909 --> 00:20:55.590
individuals and

00:20:55.590 --> 00:21:00.080
businesses to repay their debts, leading to an

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:03.570
economic depression.  A

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:08.649
depression

00:21:08.649 --> 00:21:11.089
occurs when people realize that what they considered to be assets has disappeared.  Let's

00:21:11.089 --> 00:21:13.490
go back to the bar and think about it.  I

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:17.619
drank a beer and put it on my tab.  I promised the

00:21:17.619 --> 00:21:23.570
bartender I would pay him back later.  This is an asset for a bar.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:28.129
However, if the agreement is broken and repayment becomes impossible, the

00:21:28.129 --> 00:21:29.309
"credit" becomes a default.  This would render the

00:21:29.309 --> 00:21:32.649
bar's assets worthless.  It

00:21:32.649 --> 00:21:35.779
disappears.  The

00:21:35.779 --> 00:21:39.710
lender

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.759
agrees to restructure the debt in order to avoid the loss of the asset.

00:21:40.759 --> 00:21:44.320
However, in that case, the repayment amount will be reduced, the

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:48.049
repayment period will be extended, or the

00:21:48.049 --> 00:21:52.330
interest rate that was initially agreed upon will be lowered.  The

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:56.889
contract is terminated to reduce the debt, but the lender would rather

00:21:56.889 --> 00:21:59.419
recover some money than have nothing repaid at all.  Even if

00:21:59.419 --> 00:22:03.450
the debt is extinguished, if the debt is restructured,

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:06.559
income and asset values ​​will decrease rapidly, and the

00:22:06.559 --> 00:22:09.679
debt burden ratio will worsen even further.

00:22:09.679 --> 00:22:12.950
Reducing expenses is difficult, but

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:16.009
reducing debt is also very challenging.

00:22:16.009 --> 00:22:21.940
This will also affect the central government.  As incomes decrease and employment declines, the amount of

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:27.049
taxes paid to the government will also decrease.

00:22:27.049 --> 00:22:30.210
Furthermore, with unemployment rising, the government needs to increase spending.

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:33.960
Many unemployed people have no savings and

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:36.419
need government assistance.  The

00:22:36.419 --> 00:22:39.999
government also tries to stimulate the economy by

00:22:39.999 --> 00:22:43.879
increasing spending and restoring its strength.

00:22:43.879 --> 00:22:47.509
When leverage disappears, the

00:22:47.509 --> 00:22:51.059
government's budget burden increases sharply simply because tax revenues have decreased.

00:22:51.059 --> 00:22:55.720
This is the reason for the increase in the government's debt burden.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:01.320
To repay this debt, we would need to either increase tax revenue or

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:06.059
increase borrowing, but with declining incomes and rising unemployment, there are no

00:23:06.059 --> 00:23:09.789
sources of income.

00:23:09.789 --> 00:23:14.580
Then the government tries to collect money from the wealthy.

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:17.109
Assets are held by a limited number of people.  The

00:23:17.109 --> 00:23:20.379
government will increase tax revenue from these wealthy individuals.

00:23:20.379 --> 00:23:24.450
Then wealth redistribution occurs.

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:29.279
From those who have to those who do not.  Poor people tend to

00:23:29.279 --> 00:23:30.970
dislike the wealthy.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:36.309
Furthermore, the wealthy tend to resent the poor due to economic weakening, a collapse in asset values, and

00:23:36.309 --> 00:23:39.940
increased taxes.  If the

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:43.890
depression continues, social unrest will arise.

00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:47.280
Not only will domestic conflicts increase, but frustration will also be seen

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:52.200
between countries, particularly between creditor nations and debtor nations.  If

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:56.040
this situation continues, a political upheaval could occur, leading to a very

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:58.840
serious situation.

00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:02.630
In the 1930s, this led to Hitler's rise to power,

00:24:02.630 --> 00:24:08.080
war in Europe, and the Great Depression in America.

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:10.070
Therefore, strong countermeasures became necessary, as what

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:14.950
ordinary people thought was money was actually credit.

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:18.400
And when the credits expired, I found myself short of money.

00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:23.190
People needed money.  Who can print money?  It

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:27.370
is the central bank.

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:30.309
Since interest rates had fallen to zero, there was

00:24:30.309 --> 00:24:34.090
no other option but to print money.

00:24:34.090 --> 00:24:37.299
Compared to reducing spending and redistributing wealth,

00:24:37.299 --> 00:24:42.190
printing money stimulates the economy by causing inflation.  The

00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:43.210
central bank prints new currency out of thin air,

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:47.150
buys assets, and purchases government bonds.

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:52.260
This happened during the Great Depression in the United States, and it also

00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:56.010
happened again in 2008.  The Federal Reserve, the central bank of the United States, has

00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:59.940
printed more than $2 trillion in new money.

00:24:59.940 --> 00:25:04.179
Other central banks around the world also printed as much money as they could.

00:25:04.179 --> 00:25:07.440
Buying financial assets with this will

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:11.679
drive up asset prices and make borrowing easier.

00:25:11.679 --> 00:25:15.820
However, this would only help those who own financial assets.

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:21.840
Central banks can print money, but they can only purchase financial assets.  On the

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:24.900
other hand, the central government

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:29.580
can buy goods and services and put that money into the pockets of the people.

00:25:29.580 --> 00:25:34.520
But you can't print money.

00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:35.650
Therefore, cooperation between both parties is necessary to revitalize the economy.  When a

00:25:35.650 --> 00:25:40.470
central bank purchases government bonds, it is essentially

00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:41.190
lending money to the government, which then

00:25:41.190 --> 00:25:44.909
increases spending on goods and services through deficit budgets,

00:25:44.909 --> 00:25:48.650
stimulates the economy, and

00:25:48.650 --> 00:25:53.080
pays unemployment benefits.  This would increase national income and also

00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:56.240
increase the national deficit.  But

00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:59.540
this will reduce the total debt burden on the economy.

00:25:59.540 --> 00:26:05.429
This involves risks.  It is important for the government to balance four methods to

00:26:05.429 --> 00:26:06.590
reduce debt.

00:26:06.590 --> 00:26:13.050
Maintaining a balance between deflationary and inflationary factors

00:26:13.050 --> 00:26:14.710
contributes to economic stability.

00:26:14.710 --> 00:26:18.130
If this balance can be achieved,

00:26:18.130 --> 00:26:21.479
reducing leverage will yield positive results.

00:26:21.479 --> 00:26:25.359
Reducing leverage can lead to either negative or positive results.  In

00:26:25.359 --> 00:26:28.839
what situations is it beneficial to reduce leverage?

00:26:28.839 --> 00:26:33.429
This is a difficult situation, but

00:26:33.429 --> 00:26:37.549
if we can handle it well, a good outcome is possible.

00:26:37.549 --> 00:26:42.210
This is better than the unbalanced and excessive leverage caused by debt, in

00:26:42.210 --> 00:26:45.940
which case

00:26:45.940 --> 00:26:51.089
debt decreases relative to income, the real economy improves, and

00:26:51.089 --> 00:26:56.889
inflation problems are resolved.  This is the case when balance is achieved.  To achieve

00:26:56.889 --> 00:27:00.159
this balance, economic and social stability can be maintained by skillfully controlling

00:27:00.159 --> 00:27:04.229
spending, reducing debt, redistributing wealth, and

00:27:04.229 --> 00:27:09.149
printing money.  I'm often

00:27:09.149 --> 00:27:13.639
asked whether printing money will cause inflation.

00:27:13.639 --> 00:27:18.879
If that can offset the collapse of credit, then there will be no inflation.

00:27:18.879 --> 00:27:24.249
Whether you pay with cash or by credit, the

00:27:24.249 --> 00:27:25.969
increase in spending remains the same.  The

00:27:25.969 --> 00:27:31.299
central bank can print money and use the increased money to

00:27:31.299 --> 00:27:33.080
compensate for the decreasing credit.

00:27:33.080 --> 00:27:38.509
To stimulate the economy, central banks need to ensure that

00:27:38.509 --> 00:27:39.519
when incomes increase, the

00:27:39.519 --> 00:27:43.849
rate of income growth outpaces the rate of interest on accumulated debt

00:27:43.849 --> 00:27:45.099
.

00:27:45.099 --> 00:27:48.379
What does this mean?

00:27:48.379 --> 00:27:52.309
Basically, your income needs to grow faster than your debt.  Let's

00:27:52.309 --> 00:27:56.080
assume there is a country where leverage is decreasing.  Let's assume

00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:58.580
this debt-to-income ratio is 100%.  This means that

00:27:58.580 --> 00:28:03.659
the country's total annual income will be equal to its existing debt

00:28:03.659 --> 00:28:05.799
.  Let's assume

00:28:05.799 --> 00:28:09.009
this debt accrues interest.  Let's

00:28:09.009 --> 00:28:11.159
assume the interest rate is 2%.  Because of

00:28:11.159 --> 00:28:15.029
this interest rate, if debt is increasing at a rate of 2% while

00:28:15.029 --> 00:28:15.690


00:28:15.690 --> 00:28:20.230
income is growing at a rate of 1%, it becomes impossible to repay the debt.

00:28:20.230 --> 00:28:24.809
To make income growth higher than the interest rate, we need to print enough money

00:28:24.809 --> 00:28:25.950
.

00:28:25.950 --> 00:28:30.720
However, printing money is easy, making it susceptible to misuse, and

00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:33.049
citizens often desire it.  The

00:28:33.049 --> 00:28:36.200
important thing is to avoid

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:41.110
printing a massive amount of money and

00:28:41.110 --> 00:28:43.129
causing hyperinflation, as happened in Germany in the 1920s.

00:28:43.129 --> 00:28:48.269
If the government can maintain a balance, the problem will not worsen.

00:28:48.269 --> 00:28:51.340
Even with a low growth rate, debt will decrease.

00:28:51.340 --> 00:28:54.470
This is possible even with reduced leverage.

00:28:54.470 --> 00:28:59.830
As income increases, a borrower's creditworthiness improves.

00:28:59.830 --> 00:29:02.999
As a result, lenders will start lending

00:29:02.999 --> 00:29:08.509
money, and the debt burden will begin to decrease.

00:29:08.509 --> 00:29:13.499
If people can borrow money, spending will increase, and the

00:29:13.499 --> 00:29:14.399
economy will grow.

00:29:14.399 --> 00:29:18.009
This corresponds to the reflationary stage in the long-term debt cycle.  A

00:29:18.009 --> 00:29:22.490
reduction in leverage can become a major problem if handled incorrectly, but if

00:29:22.490 --> 00:29:26.279
handled correctly, it can lead to problem resolution.  It will take

00:29:26.279 --> 00:29:29.580


00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:33.669
more than 10 years for the debt burden to decrease and for economic activity to return to normal.

00:29:33.669 --> 00:29:37.899
Therefore, it is called the "lost decade."

00:29:37.899 --> 00:29:42.720
Of course, the workings of the economy are not as simple as they appear here

00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:43.639
.

00:29:43.639 --> 00:29:48.850
However, if we superimpose the short-term debt cycle onto the long-term debt cycle, and then

00:29:48.850 --> 00:29:52.629
superimpose that onto the productivity growth curve, we can begin to

00:29:52.629 --> 00:29:55.919
understand the meaning of our past experiences.  We can

00:29:55.919 --> 00:29:58.919
understand the current situation and predict the future.  To

00:29:58.919 --> 00:30:03.019
summarize, there are three important elements.

00:30:03.019 --> 00:30:03.720
Please remember the following:

00:30:03.720 --> 00:30:08.220
Firstly, do not let your debt increase faster than your income.

00:30:08.220 --> 00:30:11.429
Otherwise, the debt burden will become unbearable.

00:30:11.429 --> 00:30:16.059
Secondly, do not increase income faster than productivity.

00:30:16.059 --> 00:30:19.159
That would weaken their competitiveness.

00:30:19.159 --> 00:30:24.000
Thirdly, we must spare no effort in improving productivity.

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:29.029
This is the most important factor in the long run.

00:30:29.549 --> 00:30:34.080
This is a useful model for everyone, including policymakers.  You might be

00:30:34.080 --> 00:30:38.470
surprised, but most people, and most policymakers, don't

00:30:38.470 --> 00:30:39.509
realize how important this is.

00:30:39.509 --> 00:30:44.059
This model was helpful to me, and I hope it will be helpful to you as well.

00:30:44.059 --> 00:30:46.380
thank you very much.

